.TH SYNC 1
.SH NAME
sync \- write everything to the disk now
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sync
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It asks the file server to commit now what was written, instead of at its
next regular commit.
.BR poweroff (8)
and
.B reboot
do it themselves.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR fs (4),
.BR poweroff (8)
